  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "${lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{\\theta \\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta }=$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we can simplify the limit using trigonometric identities, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{\\theta \\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta } & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{\\theta }\u00f7\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta ) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{\\theta }\u00f7\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta ) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }{\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta ) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }{\\theta }\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate the limits separately:\n\n- Consider the first limit. Notice that as $\\theta \\to 0,$ both numerator and denominator approach $0.$ \n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }=\\frac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form. \n\nInstead, let's recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider the second limit. Evaluating it directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}\u20610=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }{\\theta }\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta  & =1\\cdot 1=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
